[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:11. One Good Turn Deserves Another]
[00:00.680] Passage 11 | 文章十一
[00:02.440] One good turn deserves another. | 礼尚往来。
[00:06.480] I was having dinner at a restaurant, | 我正在一家餐馆吃饭，
[00:09.815] when Harry Steel came in. | 碰巧哈里·斯蒂尔走了进来。
[00:12.215] Harry worked in a lawyer's office years ago, | 哈里多年前曾在一家律师事务所工作，
[00:15.685] but he is now working at a bank. | 但他现在在一家银行上班。
[00:18.515] He gets a good salary, | 他薪水很高，
[00:20.925] but he always borrows money from his friends, | 但他总是向朋友借钱，
[00:24.000] and never pays it back. | 从来不还。
[00:26.520] Harry saw me and came and sat at the same table. | 哈里看到我，就走过来坐在了同一张桌子旁。
[00:31.300] He has never borrowed money from me. | 他从没向我借过钱。
[00:34.610] While he was eating, | 他吃饭的时候，
[00:36.950] I asked him to lend me two pounds. | 我问他借给我两英镑。
[00:40.305] To my surprise, | 令我吃惊的是，
[00:42.120] he gave me the money immediately. | 他立刻就把钱给了我。
[00:44.735] "I have never borrowed any money from you," Harry said, | “我可从来没向你借过钱，”哈里说，
[00:49.070] "So now, | “所以现在，
[00:50.680] you can pay for my dinner." | 你可以替我付饭钱了。”